{"title":"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(quick_and_ez)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(quick and ez)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Right <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/9220fbf9b857057ce8ebf126a73345075914fca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=3, BC=4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de655228c3d678063f24bb8b8b4acea69c06e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=5.$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> Square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b19f8dbfc953dc92e24445d3a1b26f5fd120eff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZW$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is inscribed in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66e3c8aa5c0ff967ac6e36ae99795caf4117b7ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}, W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"19\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f694ab8315c055ae7dd5d9fe5ba57a1a7c97a99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a54a3be7e759a747245725fab3ded3d9e2e2540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> What is the side length of the square?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/0392ede8ff49cd688062dd92d84ea7abac0569a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{3}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{60}{37} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{12}{7} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{23}{13} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"389\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2007AMC10B21.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/da/2007AMC10B21.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"347\" height=\"208\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>There are lots of similar triangles in the diagram, but we will only use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473e185ef7fd5cdcfabeac6d4bf7ee967c9a0da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle WBZ \\sim \\triangle ABC.$\" width=\"150\" height=\"13\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the sidelength of the square, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb9f00d4cda9d17ac0047e45340885204b2f828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h-s$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> is the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b71133f5874e8f7d9ecac40f95ba5724a68724f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WZ.$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> By similar triangles,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f2cd4d1a12cb4a8133a2286a3a741a0905da70e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{h-s}{h}&amp;=\\frac{s}{5}\\\\ 5(h-s)&amp;=hs\\\\ 5h-5s&amp;=hs\\\\ 5h&amp;=s(h+5)\\\\ s&amp;=\\frac{5h}{h+5} \\end{align*}\" width=\"151\" height=\"159\" />\n</p><p>Find the length of the altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> Since it is a right triangle, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db0dbc4cac70485f532703143d1b0c995e43b86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(3)(4) = 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The area can also be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378343a4ce08678cddcd727c7deb74f634a3497f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(5)(h),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e855ca6250b8e88f422f008b4b7d3004c8027f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2}h=6 \\longrightarrow h=2.4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"157\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Substitute back into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d9c01a214955f96b174391be96b26abf545cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/2428823e03c93fa3658d6a943a086222219dd6eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s=\\frac{5h}{h+5} = \\frac{12}{7.4} = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\frac{60}{37}}\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the side length of the inscribed square. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad6d92d74708cbe89ca4498e213a4baf9d6bd97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ZYC \\sim \\triangle WBZ \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" width=\"230\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Then we can setup the following ratios:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/7204a7763a44bff02492d4aeabcdd6ccccb0a685.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{CZ}{l} = \\frac{5}{3} \\rightarrow CZ = \\frac{5}{3}l\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/9/0295445dd41ed387652802a841dc47f2f39d511d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{ZB}{l} = \\frac{4}{5} \\rightarrow ZB = \\frac{4}{5}l\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>But then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e9e434cb5d8af8f591079117d2ddd69447f94ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{3}l+\\frac{4}{5}l = CZ+ZB = CB = 4 \\longrightarrow \\frac{37}{15}l=4 \\longrightarrow l = \\frac{60}{37} \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\frac{60}{37}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"542\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28quick_and_ez.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(quick_and_ez)\">Solution 3(quick and ez)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(quick and ez)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After drawing the figure, realize that triangle ABC is similar to AXY, so then, we know that if we call line segment XW 4d, AW must be 5d, so BW=3-5d and since line segment WZ is still 4d since WXYZ is a square, so since triangle WBZ is still similar to triangle ABC, (3-5d)/(4d) must equal 3/5, so solving, we get d=15/37 and that the value of 4d, or what we are looking for, is 60/37, or the answer B. \n</p><p>-Michaellin16\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=4662\">https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=4662</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B\">2007 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017144936\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.045 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 270/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6207/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.347      1 -total\n 69.06%   11.290      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 30.18%    4.933      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9470:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017144936 and revision id 278647. Rendering was triggered because: api-pars